                %path{:d => "M -4.14546 4.782166 C -3.386304 1.913536 -1.698995 0.556857 0.000597345 -0.00158934 C -1.69959 -0.559877 -3.386153 -1.911825 -4.145641 -4.783116 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.79701;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.954782,-0.283841,-0.283841,-0.954782,156.448197,57.908808)"}
                %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                  %use{:x => "98.92687", "xlink:href" => "#Fc5Qn0nnoBbqWzDdeDHSzvccdrQ=-glyph2-3", :y => "86.702524"}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_m
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernel#kernels_from_deterministic_functions"} kernel induced by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            has the same entries as
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is indeed measurable for the sigma-algebra of invariant sets.
          %p
            Note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi inv
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_inv
            is
            %em not
            the colimit simply in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meas"} category of measurable functions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+kernels"} zero-one kernels
          %p
            In the category of kernels, the set-theoretic quotient and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi inv
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_inv
            are isomorphic. This can be seen from the fact that Markov kernels are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+morphisms"} Kleisli morphisms
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meas"} Meas
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints+preserve+colimits"} left adjoints preserve colimits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+kernels"} zero-one kernels
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+measure#the_monad_of_zeroone_measures"} sobrification monad
          %h3#for_stochastic_actions For stochastic actions
          %p
            A monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            can also act stochastically on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernels"} Markov kernels
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_m:X\to X
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            and all measurable
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi A
                            %mo ;
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∉
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k_m(A|x) \;=\; 1_A(x) \;=\; \begin{cases}
                  1 &amp; x\in A ; \\
                  0 &amp; x\notin A ,
                  \\end{cases}
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k_{m\cdot n}(A|x) \;=\; \int_X k_m(A|x')\,k_n(d x'|x) .
          %p
            (This is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %mi Stoch
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B M\to Stoch
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+measure#categorytheoretic_description"} invariant measure
          %p
            In this case, an
            %strong invariant set
            is a measurable set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi A
                            %mo ;
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∉
                            %mi A
                            %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k(A|x) \;=\; 1_A(x) \;=\; \begin{cases}
                  1 &amp; x\in A ; \\
                  0 &amp; x\notin A .
                  \\end{cases}
          %p These sets form again a sigma-algebra, generalizing the case of actions via functions.
          %p
            This sigma-algebra is in general
            %em not
            a colimit in a category of kernels (
            %a{:href => "#ergodic_dagger"}> EP’23
            , Example 3.9). See however the almost sure case
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#almost_surely_invariant_sets"} below
          %h3#almost_surely_invariant_sets Almost surely invariant sets
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+measure"} stationary
            actions, i.e. for actions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+space"} probability space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,p)
            via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure-preserving+functions"} measure-preserving functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+measure"} invariant measure
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong almost surely invariant set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq X
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∖
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∖
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p(A\setminus m^{-1}(A)) \;=\; p(m^{-1}(A)\setminus A) \;=\; 0 .
          %p
            Equivalently, if for all measurable
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\subseteq X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∩
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p(S\cap m^{-1}(A)) \;=\; p(S\cap A) .
          %p
            More generally, if we have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernel#measurepreserving_kernels"} measure-preserving kernels
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_m:(X,p)\to(X,p)
            %strong almost surely invariant
            a measurable subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq X
            such that for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi A
                            %mo ;
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∉
                            %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k_m(A|x) \;=\; 1_A(x) \;=\; \begin{cases}
                  1 &amp; x\in A ; \\
                  0 &amp; x\notin A
                  \\end{cases}
          %p
            for
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              \-almost all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\subseteq X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int_S k_m(A|x) \,p(d x) \;=\; p(S\cap A) .
          %p
            These sets form again a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebra"} sigma-algebra
            %strong almost surely invariant sigma-algebra
            (or sometimes, possibly confusingly, again
            = succeed ")." do
              %strong invariant sigma-algebra
          %p
            Similarly to the deterministic case, this sigma-algebra is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            of the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+couplings"} category of couplings
            (
            %a{:href => "#ergodic_dagger"}> EP’23
            , Section 3.1).
          %h3#further_properties Further properties
          %ul
            %li
              By definition, every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+measure"} ergodic measure
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+measure"} zero-one
              on invariant sets.
            %li
              The
              %span.newWikiWord
                ergodic theorem
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/ergodic+theorem"} ?
              says that, in some cases,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empirical+means"} empirical means
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+variables"} random variables
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stationary+system"} stationary system
              tend to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conditional+expectations"} conditional expectations
              w.r.t. the invariant sigma-algebra.
